<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Acer gets US$12 mln Italian order.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Acer gets US$12 mln Italian order.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's computer giant Acer Inc said on Thursday it had received computer orders worth some US$12 million from the Italian government.</p>
<p>Italy's telecommunications bureau has decided to buy 5,000 personal computers from Acer after a hotly contested auction involving several major European computer makers, Acer said in a statement.</p>
<p>Acer said the purchase was its second major order in Europe following the sale of 25,000 computers to the Netherlands' tax bureau in January.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
